{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vue Query is now written in "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"TypeScript"}]},{"type":"text","value":" to make sure the library and your projects are type-safe!"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Things to keep in mind:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Types currently require using TypeScript v4.1 or greater"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Changes to types in this repository are considered "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"non-breaking"}]},{"type":"text","value":" and are usually released as "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"patch"}]},{"type":"text","value":" semver changes (otherwise every type enhancement would be a major version!)."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"It is "},{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"highly recommended that you lock your vue-query package version to a specific patch release and upgrade with the expectation that types may be fixed or upgraded between any release"}]}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The non-type-related public API of Vue Query still follows semver very strictly."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-inference","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Inference"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Types in Vue Query generally flow through very well so that you don't have to provide type annotations for yourself"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const { data } = useQuery({\n  //    ^? const data: Ref<number> | Ref<undefined>\n  queryKey: ['test'],\n  queryFn: () => Promise.resolve(5),\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://www.typescriptlang.org/play?#code/JYWwDg9gTgLgBAbzgVwM4FMCKz1QJ5wC+cAZlBCHAOQACMAhgHaoMDGA1gPQBuOAtAEcc+KgFgAUBNYRm8JABN6DInAC8KDNlx4AFAglw4nTocMA9APwG4Q7QGl0eAFxwA2lRjoWVALoAaa1t8ADFGFx0ASjUAPjgABXIQYAwAOigvCAAbbnQdAFYIgPFCCKA","children":[{"type":"text","value":"typescript playground"}]}]},{"type":"code","value":"const { data } = useQuery({\n  //      ^? const data: Ref<string> | Ref<undefined>\n  queryKey: ['test'],\n  queryFn: () => Promise.resolve(5),\n  select: (data) => data.toString(),\n})","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://www.typescriptlang.org/play?#code/JYWwDg9gTgLgBAbzgVwM4FMCKz1QJ5wC+cAZlBCHAOQACMAhgHaoMDGA1gPQBuOAtAEcc+KgFgAUBNYRm8JABN6DInAC8KDNlx4AFAglw4nTodNwAegH4DcIdoDS6PAC44AbSox0LKgF0ANDZ2+ABijK46AJRqAHxwAArkIMAYAHRQ3hAANtzoOgCskYHihhhZ6KwwEYoM0apxNfSpMBAAyjBQwIwA5lHFhJFAA","children":[{"type":"text","value":"typescript playground"}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This works best if your "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"queryFn"},{"type":"text","value":" has a well-defined returned type. Keep in mind that most data fetching libraries return "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"any"},{"type":"text","value":" per default, so make sure to extract it to a properly typed function:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const fetchGroups = (): Promise<Group[]> =>\n  axios.get('/groups').then((response) => response.data)\n\nconst { data } = useQuery({ queryKey: ['groups'], queryFn: fetchGroups })\n//      ^? const data: Ref<Group[]> | Ref<undefined>","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://www.typescriptlang.org/play?#-EA","children":[{"type":"text","value":"typescript playground"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"type-narrowing","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Type Narrowing"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Vue Query uses a "},{"type":"link","href":"https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/typescript-in-5-minutes-func.html#discriminated-unions","children":[{"type":"text","value":"discriminated union type"}]},{"type":"text","value":" for the query result, discriminated by the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"},{"type":"text","value":" field and the derived status boolean flags. This will allow you to check for e.g. "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"success"},{"type":"text","value":" status to make "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data"},{"type":"text","value":" defined:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const { data, isSuccess } = reactive(\n  useQuery({\n    queryKey: ['test'],\n    queryFn: () => Promise.resolve(5),\n  }),\n)\n\nif (isSuccess) {\n  data\n  // ^? const data: number\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://www.typescriptlang.org/play?#code/JYWwDg9gTgLgBAbzgVwM4FMCKz1QJ5wC+cAZlBCHAOQACMAhgHaoMDGA1gPQBuOAtAEcc+KgFgAUKEixEcKOnqsYwbuiKlylKr3RUA3BImsIzeEgAm9BgBo4wVAGVkrVulSp1AXjkKlK9AAUaFjCeAEA2lQwbjBUALq2AQCUcJ4AfHAACpr26AB08qgQADaqAQCsSVWGkiRwAfZOLm6oKQgScJ1wlgwSnJydAHoA-BKEEkA","children":[{"type":"text","value":"typescript playground"}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"typing-the-error-field","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Typing the error field"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The type for error defaults to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"unknown"},{"type":"text","value":". This is in line with what TypeScript gives you per default in a catch clauses (see "},{"type":"link","href":"https://devblogs.microsoft.com/typescript/announcing-typescript-4-4/#use-unknown-catch-variables","children":[{"type":"text","value":"useUnknownInCatchVariables"}]},{"type":"text","value":"). The safest way to work with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error"},{"type":"text","value":" would be to perform a runtime check; another way would be to explicitly define types for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"data"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"error"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"const { error } = useQuery({ queryKey: ['groups'], queryFn: fetchGroups })\n//      ^? const error: Ref<unknown>\n\nif (error.value instanceof Error) {\n  error.value\n  //     ^? const error: Error\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"link","href":"https://www.typescriptlang.org/play?#code/JYWwDg9gTgLgBAbzgVwM4FMCKz1QJ5wC+cAZlBCHAOQACMAhgHaoMDGA1gPQBuOAtAEcc+KgFgAUKEiw49AB7AIqUuUpV5i1GPESYeMOjgBxcsjBwAvIjjAAJgC44jZCABGuIhImsIzeCXQYVgALEwgzZSsACgBKRwAFVWAMAB4wswBtAF0APks8jSUAOgBzQKiqThLTMC0Yophg9EYoqHRUSGZDCzy2jt8MItt6BhivcR8-a1xyKCJLFAxsXDwopCEVgGl0PEcMqmrw2qosgBo4DfwAMUZHAKDQmuVCMfFOTjhPr4A9AH44SYsOAzaCOABK6BIKWQjHYjAgAHdGDlxsASHAoiCoEVuPQADY4Gx+JisdAQdEAUSgsxiiAknyxOPxOHpcHeX0+fwBA3gWMcVNmEkIQA","children":[{"type":"text","value":"typescript playground"}]}]}],"headings":[{"id":"type-inference","text":"Type Inference","level":2},{"id":"type-narrowing","text":"Type Narrowing","level":2},{"id":"typing-the-error-field","text":"Typing the error field","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nVue Query is now written in **TypeScript** to make sure the library and your projects are type-safe!\n\nThings to keep in mind:\n\n- Types currently require using TypeScript v4.1 or greater\n- Changes to types in this repository are considered **non-breaking** and are usually released as **patch** semver changes (otherwise every type enhancement would be a major version!).\n- It is **highly recommended that you lock your vue-query package version to a specific patch release and upgrade with the expectation that types may be fixed or upgraded between any release**\n- The non-type-related public API of Vue Query still follows semver very strictly.\n\n## Type Inference\n\nTypes in Vue Query generally flow through very well so that you don't have to provide type annotations for yourself\n\n\n\n```tsx\nconst { data } = useQuery({\n  //    ^? const data: Ref<number> | Ref<undefined>\n  queryKey: ['test'],\n  queryFn: () => Promise.resolve(5),\n})\n```\n\n[typescript playground](https://www.typescriptlang.org/play?#code/JYWwDg9gTgLgBAbzgVwM4FMCKz1QJ5wC+cAZlBCHAOQACMAhgHaoMDGA1gPQBuOAtAEcc+KgFgAUBNYRm8JABN6DInAC8KDNlx4AFAglw4nTocMA9APwG4Q7QGl0eAFxwA2lRjoWVALoAaa1t8ADFGFx0ASjUAPjgABXIQYAwAOigvCAAbbnQdAFYIgPFCCKA)\n\n\n\n\n```tsx\nconst { data } = useQuery({\n  //      ^? const data: Ref<string> | Ref<undefined>\n  queryKey: ['test'],\n  queryFn: () => Promise.resolve(5),\n  select: (data) => data.toString(),\n})\n```\n\n[typescript playground](https://www.typescriptlang.org/play?#code/JYWwDg9gTgLgBAbzgVwM4FMCKz1QJ5wC+cAZlBCHAOQACMAhgHaoMDGA1gPQBuOAtAEcc+KgFgAUBNYRm8JABN6DInAC8KDNlx4AFAglw4nTodNwAegH4DcIdoDS6PAC44AbSox0LKgF0ANDZ2+ABijK46AJRqAHxwAArkIMAYAHRQ3hAANtzoOgCskYHihhhZ6KwwEYoM0apxNfSpMBAAyjBQwIwA5lHFhJFAA)\n\n\n\nThis works best if your `queryFn` has a well-defined returned type. Keep in mind that most data fetching libraries return `any` per default, so make sure to extract it to a properly typed function:\n\n\n\n```tsx\nconst fetchGroups = (): Promise<Group[]> =>\n  axios.get('/groups').then((response) => response.data)\n\nconst { data } = useQuery({ queryKey: ['groups'], queryFn: fetchGroups })\n//      ^? const data: Ref<Group[]> | Ref<undefined>\n```\n\n[typescript playground](https://www.typescriptlang.org/play?#-EA)\n\n\n\n## Type Narrowing\n\nVue Query uses a [discriminated union type](https://www.typescriptlang.org/docs/handbook/typescript-in-5-minutes-func.html#discriminated-unions) for the query result, discriminated by the `status` field and the derived status boolean flags. This will allow you to check for e.g. `success` status to make `data` defined:\n\n\n\n```tsx\nconst { data, isSuccess } = reactive(\n  useQuery({\n    queryKey: ['test'],\n    queryFn: () => Promise.resolve(5),\n  }),\n)\n\nif (isSuccess) {\n  data\n  // ^? const data: number\n}\n```\n\n[typescript playground](https://www.typescriptlang.org/play?#code/JYWwDg9gTgLgBAbzgVwM4FMCKz1QJ5wC+cAZlBCHAOQACMAhgHaoMDGA1gPQBuOAtAEcc+KgFgAUKEixEcKOnqsYwbuiKlylKr3RUA3BImsIzeEgAm9BgBo4wVAGVkrVulSp1AXjkKlK9AAUaFjCeAEA2lQwbjBUALq2AQCUcJ4AfHAACpr26AB08qgQADaqAQCsSVWGkiRwAfZOLm6oKQgScJ1wlgwSnJydAHoA-BKEEkA)\n\n\n\n## Typing the error field\n\nThe type for error defaults to `unknown`. This is in line with what TypeScript gives you per default in a catch clauses (see [useUnknownInCatchVariables](https://devblogs.microsoft.com/typescript/announcing-typescript-4-4/#use-unknown-catch-variables)). The safest way to work with `error` would be to perform a runtime check; another way would be to explicitly define types for `data` and `error`:\n\n\n\n```tsx\nconst { error } = useQuery({ queryKey: ['groups'], queryFn: fetchGroups })\n//      ^? const error: Ref<unknown>\n\nif (error.value instanceof Error) {\n  error.value\n  //     ^? const error: Error\n}\n```\n\n[typescript playground](https://www.typescriptlang.org/play?#code/JYWwDg9gTgLgBAbzgVwM4FMCKz1QJ5wC+cAZlBCHAOQACMAhgHaoMDGA1gPQBuOAtAEcc+KgFgAUKEiw49AB7AIqUuUpV5i1GPESYeMOjgBxcsjBwAvIjjAAJgC44jZCABGuIhImsIzeCXQYVgALEwgzZSsACgBKRwAFVWAMAB4wswBtAF0APks8jSUAOgBzQKiqThLTMC0Yophg9EYoqHRUSGZDCzy2jt8MItt6BhivcR8-a1xyKCJLFAxsXDwopCEVgGl0PEcMqmrw2qosgBo4DfwAMUZHAKDQmuVCMfFOTjhPr4A9AH44SYsOAzaCOABK6BIKWQjHYjAgAHdGDlxsASHAoiCoEVuPQADY4Gx+JisdAQdEAUSgsxiiAknyxOPxOHpcHeX0+fwBA3gWMcVNmEkIQA)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\nid: typescript\ntitle: TypeScript\nref: docs/framework/react/typescript.md\nreplace:\n  { 'React': 'Vue', 'react-query package version': 'vue-query package version' }\n---\n\n[//]: # 'TypeInference1'\n\n```tsx\nconst { data } = useQuery({\n  //    ^? const data: Ref<number> | Ref<undefined>\n  queryKey: ['test'],\n  queryFn: () => Promise.resolve(5),\n})\n```\n\n[typescript playground](https://www.typescriptlang.org/play?#code/JYWwDg9gTgLgBAbzgVwM4FMCKz1QJ5wC+cAZlBCHAOQACMAhgHaoMDGA1gPQBuOAtAEcc+KgFgAUBNYRm8JABN6DInAC8KDNlx4AFAglw4nTocMA9APwG4Q7QGl0eAFxwA2lRjoWVALoAaa1t8ADFGFx0ASjUAPjgABXIQYAwAOigvCAAbbnQdAFYIgPFCCKA)\n\n[//]: # 'TypeInference1'\n[//]: # 'TypeInference2'\n\n```tsx\nconst { data } = useQuery({\n  //      ^? const data: Ref<string> | Ref<undefined>\n  queryKey: ['test'],\n  queryFn: () => Promise.resolve(5),\n  select: (data) => data.toString(),\n})\n```\n\n[typescript playground](https://www.typescriptlang.org/play?#code/JYWwDg9gTgLgBAbzgVwM4FMCKz1QJ5wC+cAZlBCHAOQACMAhgHaoMDGA1gPQBuOAtAEcc+KgFgAUBNYRm8JABN6DInAC8KDNlx4AFAglw4nTodNwAegH4DcIdoDS6PAC44AbSox0LKgF0ANDZ2+ABijK46AJRqAHxwAArkIMAYAHRQ3hAANtzoOgCskYHihhhZ6KwwEYoM0apxNfSpMBAAyjBQwIwA5lHFhJFAA)\n\n[//]: # 'TypeInference2'\n[//]: # 'TypeInference3'\n\n```tsx\nconst fetchGroups = (): Promise<Group[]> =>\n  axios.get('/groups').then((response) => response.data)\n\nconst { data } = useQuery({ queryKey: ['groups'], queryFn: fetchGroups })\n//      ^? const data: Ref<Group[]> | Ref<undefined>\n```\n\n[typescript playground](https://www.typescriptlang.org/play?#-EA)\n\n[//]: # 'TypeInference3'\n[//]: # 'TypeNarrowing'\n\n```tsx\nconst { data, isSuccess } = reactive(\n  useQuery({\n    queryKey: ['test'],\n    queryFn: () => Promise.resolve(5),\n  }),\n)\n\nif (isSuccess) {\n  data\n  // ^? const data: number\n}\n```\n\n[typescript playground](https://www.typescriptlang.org/play?#code/JYWwDg9gTgLgBAbzgVwM4FMCKz1QJ5wC+cAZlBCHAOQACMAhgHaoMDGA1gPQBuOAtAEcc+KgFgAUKEixEcKOnqsYwbuiKlylKr3RUA3BImsIzeEgAm9BgBo4wVAGVkrVulSp1AXjkKlK9AAUaFjCeAEA2lQwbjBUALq2AQCUcJ4AfHAACpr26AB08qgQADaqAQCsSVWGkiRwAfZOLm6oKQgScJ1wlgwSnJydAHoA-BKEEkA)\n\n[//]: # 'TypeNarrowing'\n[//]: # 'TypingError'\n\n```tsx\nconst { error } = useQuery({ queryKey: ['groups'], queryFn: fetchGroups })\n//      ^? const error: Ref<unknown>\n\nif (error.value instanceof Error) {\n  error.value\n  //     ^? const error: Error\n}\n```\n\n[typescript playground](https://www.typescriptlang.org/play?#code/JYWwDg9gTgLgBAbzgVwM4FMCKz1QJ5wC+cAZlBCHAOQACMAhgHaoMDGA1gPQBuOAtAEcc+KgFgAUKEiw49AB7AIqUuUpV5i1GPESYeMOjgBxcsjBwAvIjjAAJgC44jZCABGuIhImsIzeCXQYVgALEwgzZSsACgBKRwAFVWAMAB4wswBtAF0APks8jSUAOgBzQKiqThLTMC0Yophg9EYoqHRUSGZDCzy2jt8MItt6BhivcR8-a1xyKCJLFAxsXDwopCEVgGl0PEcMqmrw2qosgBo4DfwAMUZHAKDQmuVCMfFOTjhPr4A9AH44SYsOAzaCOABK6BIKWQjHYjAgAHdGDlxsASHAoiCoEVuPQADY4Gx+JisdAQdEAUSgsxiiAknyxOPxOHpcHeX0+fwBA3gWMcVNmEkIQA)\n\n[//]: # 'TypingError'\n[//]: # 'TypingError2'\n[//]: # 'TypingError2'\n[//]: # 'Materials'\n[//]: # 'Materials'\n"}
